  "content": {
    "prompt": "Recall that a predicate is a method with a Boolean return value. The Predicate interface can be used to test whether a value fulfills a property. A class implementing this interface provides an invoke method for carrying out a particular test.",
    "source_code": "public class GenericUtil\n{\n   /**\n      Finds first match.\n      @param value an array of values\n      @param pred a predicate\n      @return the first value for which pred is true\n   */\n   public static <T> ... findFirstMatch(... values, ... pred)\n   {\n      for (T value : values   )\n         if (pred.invoke(value))\n            return value;\n      return null;\n   }\n}"
  },
